@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# Level 220 Adventurer Duel Practice
+
+This plugin is the stationary, consensual duel-lifecycle POC for an Adventurer.
+
+It currently provides:
+
+- explicit `/duelpractice on|off|status` control;
+- the 15-second vicinity acknowledgement and acceptance countdown;
+- an exception limited to the exact accepted opponent;
+- normal attack attempts starting at 4 seconds and retrying every 10 ms;
+- configured Adventurer heals forced to self, safe defensive/offensive perks, and equipped weapon specials;
+- strict self/accepted-opponent action-target filtering;
+- only health/nano and Free Movement stims from the generic item lane;
+- opponent-targeted nanos and team-effect buffs held for an explicit rotation policy;
+- active movement halting, disabled area actions, and paused generic housekeeping; and
+- separate records in `AdvDuelPracticeRecords.tsv`.
+
+It intentionally does not contain a pistol or 1HE opening sequence yet. That
+rotation should be defined from the actual level-220 loadout and duel policy.
+Adventurer heal nano selections still default to off; select the desired nanos
+from `/handler` before live testing. Duel practice forces their target modes to
+Self and keeps the Adventurer team-heal line off.
+
+Enable only `ProfessionHandler.Adv.DuelPractice.dll` as the AO# plugin. Keep
+`ProfessionHandler.Generic.dll` and `Shared.dll` beside it as dependencies, but
+do not enable the standard Adventurer handler at the same time.
